{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>To my master, to Esav.</b> In this parashah you will find eight times that Yaakov called Esav 'my master,' and corresponding to them, eight kings reigned in Edom before any king reigned over the children of Israel." "<b>Thus says your servant Yaakov.</b> In order to cool his disposition he said thus to him — that is, the blessing of your father that he said, 'be a master to your brother,' was not fulfilled in me; rather, I wish to be your servant." "<b>With Lavan I sojourned.</b> Do not wonder from where all this that I have came to me, for I sojourned <b>with Lavan</b> our kinsman; had I sojourned with any other foreigner, I would have had nothing. Another interpretation: <b>With Lavan I sojourned</b> — as you know, by the command of my father and mother, so that Esav should not think it was on his account that he is fleeing. Another interpretation: that he should not harbor feelings against him for not having gone to greet him these twenty years, for he was a hired worker."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:07:02.722180437Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}